    fix(lint): pin golangci config to repo root and gate vendored configs — go_lint no longer aborts on vendor/*.go commits
    
    The GitReins go_lint arm runs `golangci-lint run --new-from-rev=HEAD~1 <dir>`
    once per changed package directory. golangci-lint 2.12.2 discovers the
    nearest config enclosing the analyzed directory, and the dependency bump in
    this commit vendored three upstream .golangci.yml files
    (go-openapi/jsonpointer, oasdiff/yaml, santhosh-tekuri/jsonschema/v6) that
    declare linters this build does not ship. Linting
    vendor/github.com/go-openapi/jsonpointer therefore aborted rc 3 with
    "Error: unknown linters: 'exhaustruct_v5'" — a hard config error, not a
    finding, so the whole arm died for any commit touching vendor/*.go.
    Control: ./internal/board answered "0 issues." rc 0.
    
    What changed:
    - repo-root .golangci.yml pins config discovery to the root (the root wins
      over any nested config) and excludes vendor/ from analysis: vendored code
      is upstream-maintained and the bumped kin-openapi/openapi3 itself carries
      5 errcheck + 3 staticcheck findings upstream, which would otherwise fail
      go_lint on every bump commit. No linter-set change for our own packages.
    - the three vendored .golangci.yml files are deleted: upstream build
      tooling, not part of the vendored API; go build is unaffected.
    - make vendor-strip removes any future vendor/**/.golangci* after
      `go mod vendor`; make vendor-check runs the new check-only gate.
    - internal/vendorcheck (mirrors internal/fmtcheck): a pure walk over
      vendor/ naming every .golangci* path; TestVendorcheck runs in-process
      against this repo tree; a fixture test plants configs in a t.TempDir()
      to prove the checker is RED-capable, not green-only.
    - wired like the sibling gates: ci.yml "Vendor-check" step with the
      byte-identical command, and the internal/workflowcheck gate-step census
      extended with the same entry.
    
    RED->GREEN evidence:
    - RED (before): golangci-lint run --new-from-rev=HEAD~1
      vendor/github.com/go-openapi/jsonpointer -> rc 3,
      "Error: unknown linters: 'exhaustruct_v5'".
    - GREEN (after): same invocation -> rc 0 "0 issues."; all 10 changed vendor
      package dirs -> rc 0 (kin-openapi/openapi3, jsonpointer,
      jsonpointer/jsonname, oasdiff/yaml, oasdiff/yaml3,
      x/text/{internal/catmsg, internal/number, language, message,
      message/catalog}).
    - new gate RED proof: planted vendor/zz-fixture/.golangci.yml ->
      make vendor-check FAILS rc 2 naming that path; fixture removed -> ok rc 0.
    
    Carries the staged dependency bump: kin-openapi v0.149.0 -> v0.152.0,
    go-openapi/jsonpointer v0.22.5 -> v1.0.2 (go-openapi/swag and jsonname
    dropped), oasdiff/yaml 0.1.1 -> 0.1.3, oasdiff/yaml3 v0.0.14 -> v0.0.16,
    golang.org/x/text v0.14.0 -> v0.43.0. Verified on this exact tree:
    go build ./... rc 0; go vet ./... rc 0; go test ./... -count=1 ok (17
    packages, full mode); make fmt-check / version-check / spec-check /
    vuln-check / cover-check / vendor-check all rc 0;
    go test -count=1 ./internal/workflowcheck ok.
    
